{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305122,"nonce":"jHJhqdbuZZwX33nXDWl8BaQ+mjo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhdOg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/5","origin":"github"},"title":"Candidate index shown to the user does not match the index used to select the source","message":"In `guess_file()` the number displayed beside each candidate comes from `enumerate(files[file_length])`:\n\n```python\nfor file_number, file in enumerate(files[file_length]):\n    ...\n    number_to_show = \" \" + str(file_number) + \" \"\n```\n\nbut hardlinked candidates are skipped without appending to `file_infos`. Selection then does:\n\n```python\nsrc_path = file_infos[int(user_input)].path\n```\n\nSo once any candidate has been filtered as a hardlink, the displayed number and the `file_infos` index diverge. Choosing \"2\" copies a different file than the one labelled 2.\n\nIn a recovery tool this silently writes the wrong source to the destination.","files":null}]}